<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nimbalkar</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Naik Nimbalkar</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Nimbalkars are a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Maratha</a> family who ruled the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jagir">jagir</a> and later princely state of Phaltan in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/satara">Satara</a> region of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharashtra">Maharashtra</a>. Claiming to have held Phaltan since the late 13th century, they are counted among the oldest Maratha houses and served the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deccan-sultanates">Deccan sultanates</a>, the Maratha kings and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peshwa">Peshwas</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shivaji">Shivaji</a>'s first wife, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saibai">Saibai</a>, was a Nimbalkar of Phaltan.</p></div>
